{
  "actors": [
    {
      "id": "clients",
      "label": "Clients",
      "role": "client",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "shedder",
      "label": "Edge shedder",
      "role": "shedder",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 62
    },
    {
      "id": "queue",
      "label": "Queue",
      "role": "queue",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "service",
      "label": "Service",
      "role": "service",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 38
    }
  ],
  "linkLabel": "request",
  "frames": [
    {
      "narration": "Normal day: 60 requests per second against a capacity of 100. The queue is empty and every answer comes back in about 100 ms, far inside the clients' 2 second timeout.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "60/s"
        },
        {
          "from": "shedder",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "admit"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "service",
          "label": "next"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "clients": "60/s",
        "queue": "0 waiting",
        "service": "60% busy"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "A spike: 300 requests per second arrive, 3 times capacity. The service can finish only 100 per second, so 200 per second more come in than go out.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "300/s"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "clients": "300/s",
        "service": "max 100/s"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "clients"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Without protection everything is accepted. The queue grows by 200 per second, so after one second the oldest request has waited 2 seconds, exactly the client timeout.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "shedder",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "accept all"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "service",
          "label": "oldest first"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "shedder": "no limit",
        "queue": "200 waiting, then 400",
        "service": "100% busy"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "queue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The death spiral: every request the service starts is already older than 2 seconds. Its caller left, so the answer goes nowhere. The service is 100% busy but goodput is near zero, and clients that retry make the queue longer still.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "service",
          "to": "clients",
          "label": "too late"
        },
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "retry"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "clients": "timed out, retrying",
        "queue": "3,000 waiting",
        "service": "100% busy, ~19 useful/s"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "service"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Now with load shedding. The edge counts requests in the system and allows at most 50, which is half a second of work at 100 per second. The 200 per second beyond that are refused at once with 503 or 429 and a Retry-After header.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "300/s"
        },
        {
          "from": "shedder",
          "to": "clients",
          "label": "503 Retry-After"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "shedder": "limit 50, sheds 200/s",
        "queue": "50 waiting",
        "clients": "fast failure"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "shedder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "Everything that is admitted waits at most about 0.5 seconds, so it is answered inside the timeout. Goodput stays near 80 to 100 per second instead of collapsing, and nothing the service does is wasted.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "shedder",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "admit 100/s"
        },
        {
          "from": "queue",
          "to": "service",
          "label": "next"
        },
        {
          "from": "service",
          "to": "clients",
          "label": "200 OK"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "queue": "50 waiting",
        "service": "100% busy, ~80 useful/s",
        "clients": "answered in 0.6 s"
      }
    },
    {
      "narration": "Not all requests are equal. Health checks and critical traffic are admitted until the limit is full and served first, while ordinary traffic is shed at half the limit. LIFO would also help by serving the newest request, whose caller is certainly still waiting.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "critical 20%"
        },
        {
          "from": "shedder",
          "to": "queue",
          "label": "front of queue"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "shedder": "ordinary shed at 25",
        "queue": "critical first"
      },
      "highlight": [
        "shedder",
        "queue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "narration": "The spike ends. The queue holds about 50 requests instead of thousands, so normal goodput returns at once. The unprotected service needed about 72 more seconds to drain its backlog after a 15 second spike.",
      "messages": [
        {
          "from": "clients",
          "to": "shedder",
          "label": "60/s"
        },
        {
          "from": "service",
          "to": "clients",
          "label": "200 OK"
        }
      ],
      "states": {
        "clients": "60/s",
        "shedder": "limit idle",
        "queue": "0 waiting",
        "service": "60% busy"
      }
    }
  ]
}
